\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces  Predictive-information model comparison. Model comparison results are shown for (a) strong and (b) weak monsoon starts. Bars show \(\Delta \)AICc relative to the lowest-AICc model within each event catalogue. The event-process baseline contains same-type event history and Cheng composite sampling resolution~\citep  {cheng2016asian}; the climate-state model further includes LR04~\citep  {lisiecki2005pliocene} and \(\ce {CO2}\)~\citep  {bereiter2015revision}; and the full predictive model adds precession phase~\citep  {laskar2004long}. Labels beginning with \(+\) denote terms added to the event-process baseline. (c,d) Nested likelihood-ratio tests for the same event catalogues. Bars show \(-\log _{10}(p)\), and the dashed line marks \(p=0.05\); bars to the right of this line are significant. In (c,d), labels are full-model versus reduced-model comparisons: \(+X\) vs \(M\) means adding \(X\) to model \(M\), whereas ``full predictive model vs \(-X\)'' is a drop-one comparison in which the reduced model omits \(X\). }}{8}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:predictive_model_comparison}{{3}{8}{}{figure.3}{}}
