\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Lagged predictive information from individual drivers. Model-based predictive-information gain, expressed as bits per event, from adding lagged LR04~\citep  {lisiecki2005pliocene}, \ce {CO2}~\citep  {bereiter2015revision}, or precession phase~\citep  {laskar2004long} to the event-process baseline containing same-type event history and sampling resolution. Darker translucent curve segments mark lags significant after Benjamini--Hochberg false-discovery-rate correction at \(q \leq 0.05\), applied within each event catalogue and driver lag family. (a) Strong monsoon starts. (b) Weak monsoon starts. Positive lags indicate that the driver is sampled from an older climate state relative to the event bin.}}{11}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:lagged-single-driver-info}{{4}{11}{}{figure.4}{}}
